            <ArticleTitle>Catheterization of coronary artery bypass graft from the descending aorta.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>103-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The increasing frequency of reoperation for coronary artery disease has led to the use of a variety of grafts. This report describes the catheter technique for selective opacification of a saphenous vein graft from the descending thoracic aorta to the posterior coronary circulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
